From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: demostanis <demostanis@protonmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Recognize batteries that are not charging

Linux power supplies can report "Not charging" while connected to AC,
including when a battery is full or held at a charge threshold. Treat that
state as charged instead of falling back to the unknown marker.
---
 widgets/bat_linux.lua | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/widgets/bat_linux.lua b/widgets/bat_linux.lua
--- a/widgets/bat_linux.lua
+++ b/widgets/bat_linux.lua
@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@ return helpers.setcall(function (format, warg)
     local battery_state = {
         ["Full\n"]        = "↯",
         ["Unknown\n"]     = "⌁",
+        ["Not charging\n"] = "↯",
         ["Charged\n"]     = "↯",
         ["Charging\n"]    = "+",
         ["Discharging\n"] = "-"
